676	                    "A " + claim.getStatus() + " claim cannot be reassigned");
677	        }
678	        if (!toSame && claim.getPersonId() == toPersonId) {
679	            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT, "The claim is already that person's");
680	        }
681	        refuseIfRetired(to, claim.getDate());
682	        Person from = people.findByIdAndSheetId(claim.getPersonId(), sheetId)
683	                .orElseThrow(() -> new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, "No such person"));
684	        RollupService.Snapshot before = rollup.snapshot(sheetId);
685	        if (claim.getNumber() != null && claim.getPersonId() != toPersonId) {
686	            // moved to another person: the next number in its sequence, the old one never given again
687	            retired.save(new RetiredNumber(sheetId, claim.getNumber()));
688	            claims.flush();
689	            claim.setNumber(nextNumber(sheetId, claim.getDueBy()));
690	        }
691	        claim.setPersonId(to.getId());
692	        claim.unbind();
693	        claim.setListed(claims.findLastListed(sheetId) + 1);
694	        claims.flush();
695	        record("CLAIM_REASSIGNED", user, to, claim, claim.getNumber(),
696	                " from=" + from.getName() + " to=" + to.getName());
697	        rollup.recordChanges(sheetId, user, before);
698	        return claim;
699	    }
700	
701	    /** Split an amount off an OPEN claim: the claim keeps the rest of its amount and loses any
702	     *  figure a statement bound it to, and a new OPEN claim of the amount, with the same date,
703	     *  note and tags, the next number, opened by the user, its due-by fixed now from the terms in force on
704	     *  the date (the person's own, else their grade's, else the sheet's), and naming the original's number as split-from, is listed as the person's newest (a late entry
705	     *  when a soft-closed period contains its due-by).
706	     *  Refused (404) when missing, (423) when due in a closed period, (403) for a role the
707	     *  sheet's permission matrix does not let open a claim, (409) unless OPEN and not deferred on
708	     *  the sheet's today, and (422) unless the amount is more than 0.00 and less than the claim's. */
709	    @Transactional
710	    public Split split(String sheetId, String user, long id, BigDecimal amount) {
711	        Claim claim = claims.findForUpdate(id, sheetId)
712	                .orElseThrow(() -> new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, "No such claim"));
713	        refuseIfClosed(sheetId, claim.getDueBy());
714	        settings.refuseUnlessAllowed(sheetId, user, Permission.OPEN);
715	        if (claim.getStatus() != ClaimStatus.OPEN) {
716	            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT,
717	                    "Only an OPEN claim is split, not a " + claim.getStatus() + " one");
718	        }
719	        if (claim.isDeferredOn(sheets.today(sheetId))) {
720	            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT,
721	                    "A claim deferred until " + claim.getDeferredUntil() + " cannot be split before then");
722	        }
723	        if (amount.signum() <= 0 || amount.compareTo(claim.getAmount()) >= 0) {
724	            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.UNPROCESSABLE_CONTENT,
725	                    "The amount split off must be more than 0.00 and less than the claim's");
726	        }
727	        Person person = people.findByIdAndSheetId(claim.getPersonId(), sheetId)
728	                .orElseThrow(() -> new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, "No such person"));
729	        RollupService.Snapshot before = rollup.snapshot(sheetId);
730	        LocalDate on = claim.getDate();
731	        claim.setAmount(claim.getAmount().subtract(amount));
732	        claim.unbind();
733	        int terms = termsOf(sheetId, person, on);
734	        Claim fresh = new Claim(sheetId, person.getId(), amount, on, dueByOf(sheetId, on, terms), claim.getNote());
735	        fresh.setTerms(terms);
736	        fresh.setStatus(ClaimStatus.OPEN);
737	        fresh.setNumber(nextNumber(sheetId, fresh.getDueBy()));
738	        fresh.setOpenedBy(user);
739	        fresh.setSplitFrom(claim.getNumber());
740	        fresh.setTags(claim.getTags());
741	        fresh.setLateEntry(periods.softClosedOn(sheetId, fresh.getDueBy()));
742	        fresh.setListed(claims.findLastListed(sheetId) + 1);
743	        Claim split = claims.saveAndFlush(fresh);
744	        logStatus(user, person, split);
745	        record("CLAIM_SPLIT", user, person, claim, claim.getNumber(), " into=" + split.getNumber());
746	        record("CLAIM_OPENED", user, person, split);
747	        rollup.recordChanges(sheetId, user, before);
748	        return new Split(claim, split);
749	    }
750	
751	    /** The PENDING claim a steward decides on: refused (404) when missing, (423) when dated in a
752	     *  closed period, (409) unless PENDING, and (403) when the user is not a steward. */
753	    private Claim pendingForSteward(String sheetId, String user, long id) {
754	        Claim claim = claims.findForUpdate(id, sheetId)
755	                .orElseThrow(() -> new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, "No such claim"));
756	        refuseIfClosed(sheetId, claim.getDueBy());
757	        if (claim.getStatus() != ClaimStatus.PENDING) {
758	            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT,
759	                    "Only a PENDING claim is approved or rejected, not a " + claim.getStatus() + " one");
760	        }
761	        if (settings.roleOf(sheetId, user) != Role.STEWARD) {
762	            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN,
763	                    "Only a steward approves or rejects a PENDING claim");
764	        }
765	        return claim;
766	    }
767	
768	    /** Write the claim's status now to its log: by the user, on the sheet's today, with the due
769	     *  it shows at this moment. */
770	    private void logStatus(String user, Person person, Claim claim) {
771	        BigDecimal due = shownDueOf(claim, person);
772	        log.save(new ClaimLog(claim.getSheetId(), claim.getId(), claim.getStatus(), user,
773	                sheets.today(claim.getSheetId()), due == null ? null : due.setScale(2, RoundingMode.HALF_EVEN)));
774	    }
775	
776	    private static String dueText(BigDecimal due) {
777	        return due == null ? "n/a" : due.toPlainString();
778	    }
779	
780	    /** Take a statement of a person: record their due-total now, and bind each of their claims
781	     *  that counts (OPEN, PENDING or SETTLED, but no unbound open one within a hold, nor a deferred one) to its figure now; the others
782	     *  are left unbound. Taken as of a date ({@code asOf}, not null), the sheet as it stood at the end
783	     *  of that date stands in for it now (see {@link #statementAsOf}). */
784	    @Transactional
785	    public Statement statement(String sheetId, String user, long personId, LocalDate asOf) {
786	        if (asOf != null) {
787	            return statementAsOf(sheetId, user, personId, asOf);
788	        }
789	        Person person = people.findForUpdate(personId, sheetId)
790	                .orElseThrow(() -> new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, "No such person"));
791	        LocalDate today = sheets.today(sheetId);
792	        List<Claim> theirs = claims.findByPersonForUpdate(personId, sheetId);
793	        RollupService.Snapshot before = rollup.snapshot(sheetId);
794	        List<Claim> counted = theirs.stream().filter(c -> counts(c, person, today)).toList();
795	        BigDecimal dueTotal = Sheet.capped(dueTotalOf(counted, person, today), sheets.cap(sheetId));
796	        for (Claim c : theirs) {
797	            if (counts(c, person, today)) {
798	                // the statement binds the figure; the late charge keeps following the sheet's today
799	                c.bind(c.getSettledDue() != null ? c.getSettledDue() : figureOf(c, person));
800	            } else {
801	                c.unbind();
802	            }
803	        }
804	        claims.flush();
805	        return stated(sheetId, user, person, theirs, dueTotal, counted.size(), today, null, before);
806	    }
807	
808	    /** Take a statement of a person as of a date on or before the sheet's today: their claims that
809	     *  counted at the end of it are bound to their figures as they stood then (every change made
810	     *  while the sheet's today was on or before it counts, every later one does not), with that date
811	     *  standing in for the sheet's today in every figure; their other claims are left unbound.
812	     *  Refused (422) when the date is after the sheet's today, or the person was not yet added then. */
813	    private Statement statementAsOf(String sheetId, String user, long personId, LocalDate asOf) {
814	        Person person = people.findForUpdate(personId, sheetId)
815	                .orElseThrow(() -> new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, "No such person"));
816	        LocalDate today = sheets.today(sheetId);
817	        if (asOf.isAfter(today)) {
818	            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.UNPROCESSABLE_CONTENT,
819	                    "A statement is taken as of a date on or before the sheet's today");
820	        }
821	        HistoryService.AsOf then = history.asOf(sheetId, asOf);
822	        Person was = then.people().get(personId);
823	        if (was == null) {
824	            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.UNPROCESSABLE_CONTENT,
825	                    "The person was not yet on the sheet on " + asOf);
826	        }
827	        List<Claim> theirs = claims.findByPersonForUpdate(personId, sheetId);
828	        RollupService.Snapshot before = rollup.snapshot(sheetId);
829	        RollupService.Stated stated = RollupService.statedOn(then.sheet(), was, personId,
830	                List.copyOf(then.claims().values()), RateChain.flatten(sheetId, then.rates(),
831	                        rateChain.ancestors(sheetId).stream().map(a -> history.asOf(a, asOf).rates()).toList()));
832	        Map<Long, BigDecimal> bound = new HashMap<>();
833	        then.claims().forEach((id, c) -> {
834	            if (stated.counted().containsKey(c)) {
835	                bound.put(id, stated.counted().get(c));
836	            }
837	        });
838	        for (Claim c : theirs) {
839	            if (bound.containsKey(c.getId())) {
840	                c.bind(bound.get(c.getId()));
841	            } else {
842	                c.unbind();
843	            }
844	        }
845	        claims.flush();
846	        return stated(sheetId, user, person, theirs, stated.dueTotal(), stated.counted().size(), today, asOf, before);
847	    }
848	
849	    /** Record a statement just taken (as of {@code asOf}, or null) and audit it. */
850	    private Statement stated(String sheetId, String user, Person person, List<Claim> theirs, BigDecimal dueTotal,
851	            int counted, LocalDate today, LocalDate asOf, RollupService.Snapshot before) {
852	        statements.saveAndFlush(new PersonStatement(sheetId, person.getId(), dueTotal, counted, today, asOf, user));
853	        audit.recordOnCommit("STATEMENT sheet=" + sheetId + " by=" + user + " name=" + person.getName()
854	                + " due-total=" + (dueTotal == null ? "n/a" : dueTotal.toPlainString()) + " claims=" + counted
855	                + (asOf == null ? "" : " asof=" + asOf));
856	        rollup.recordChanges(sheetId, user, before);
857	        return new Statement(person, StatementSummary.of(statements.findByPersonIdOrderByIdAsc(person.getId())), theirs);
858	    }
859	
860	    /** A steward cancels a person's last statement: it is removed, and every claim it bound is
861	     *  live again (a figure an earlier statement bound is not restored). Refused (404) when the
862	     *  person is missing, (403) for anyone but a steward, and (409) when the person has no
863	     *  statement. */
864	    @Transactional
865	    public Statement cancelStatement(String sheetId, String user, long personId) {
866	        Person person = people.findForUpdate(personId, sheetId)
867	                .orElseThrow(() -> new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, "No such person"));
868	        if (settings.roleOf(sheetId, user) != Role.STEWARD) {
869	            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN, "Only a steward cancels a statement");
870	        }
871	        List<PersonStatement> taken = statements.findByPersonIdOrderByIdAsc(personId);
872	        if (taken.isEmpty()) {
873	            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT, "The person has no statement to cancel");
874	        }
875	        PersonStatement last = taken.get(taken.size() - 1);
876	        List<Claim> theirs = claims.findByPersonForUpdate(personId, sheetId);
877	        RollupService.Snapshot before = rollup.snapshot(sheetId);
878	        theirs.forEach(Claim::unbind);
879	        claims.flush();
880	        statements.delete(last);
881	        statements.flush();
882	        audit.recordOnCommit("STATEMENT_CANCELLED sheet=" + sheetId + " by=" + user + " name=" + person.getName()
883	                + " due-total=" + (last.getDueTotal() == null ? "n/a" : last.getDueTotal().toPlainString()));
884	        rollup.recordChanges(sheetId, user, before);
885	        return new Statement(person, StatementSummary.of(statements.findByPersonIdOrderByIdAsc(personId)), theirs);
886	    }
887	
888	    /** The terms a claim of the person dated {@code on} is fixed with as it is created: the
889	     *  person's own terms, else those of their grade then in force on it, else the sheet's. */
890	    private int termsOf(String sheetId, Person person, LocalDate on) {
891	        return person.getTerms() != null ? person.getTerms()
892	                : sheets.find(sheetId).map(s -> s.termsFor(person.gradeOn(on), on)).orElse(Sheet.DEFAULT_TERMS);
893	    }
894	
895	    /** The due-by of a claim dated {@code on} with the terms: the terms-th business day after its
896	     *  date. Business days skip every Saturday, Sunday and holiday on the sheet. */
897	    private LocalDate dueByOf(String sheetId, LocalDate on, int terms) {
898	        Set<LocalDate> holidays = new HashSet<>(settings.holidays(sheetId));
899	        return BusinessDays.after(on, terms, holidays);
900	    }
901	
902	    /** A holiday just added re-fixes the due-by of every claim on the sheet that is neither SETTLED
903	     *  nor VOID and is due on or after it: from its date, with the terms it was fixed with, over the
904	     *  holidays on the sheet now. The figures that moves are recorded. */
905	    @EventListener
906	    @Transactional
907	    public void redate(HolidayAdded added) {
908	        String sheetId = added.sheetId();
909	        RollupService.Snapshot before = rollup.snapshot(sheetId);
910	        Set<LocalDate> holidays = new HashSet<>(settings.holidays(sheetId));
911	        for (Claim c : claims.findBySheetIdForUpdate(sheetId)) {
912	            if (c.getStatus() == ClaimStatus.SETTLED || c.getStatus() == ClaimStatus.VOID
913	                    || c.getDueBy().isBefore(added.day())) {
914	                continue;
915	            }
916	            c.setDueBy(BusinessDays.after(c.getDate(), c.getTerms(), holidays));
917	        }
918	        claims.flush();
919	        rollup.recordChanges(sheetId, added.user(), before);
920	    }
921	
922	    /** The number a claim due by {@code date} takes as it is opened: under period numbering (set,
923	     *  and the sheet's today on or after it) the next within the period containing the due-by
924	     *  (<period name>-<n>), or X-<n> when none does; otherwise the sheet's next number. */
925	    public String nextNumber(String sheetId, LocalDate date) {
926	        if (!sheets.periodNumberingOn(sheetId)) {
927	            return String.valueOf(sheets.nextClaimNumber(sheetId));
928	        }
929	        // held until the transaction ends, so two claims opened at once are numbered one after the other
930	        sheets.lock(sheetId);
931	        String prefix = periods.containing(sheetId, date).map(Period::getName).orElse(NO_PERIOD) + "-";
932	        List<String> given = new ArrayList<>(claims.findNumbers(sheetId));
933	        given.addAll(retired.findNumbers(sheetId));
934	        int last = given.stream()
935	                .filter(n -> n.startsWith(prefix))
936	                .map(n -> n.substring(prefix.length()))
937	                .filter(n -> n.matches("\\d{1,9}"))
938	                .mapToInt(Integer::parseInt)
939	                .max().orElse(0);
940	        return prefix + (last + 1);
941	    }
942	
943	    /** Refuse (423) a change to a claim due by a date in a closed period, holding the sheet locked until
944	     *  the transaction ends so a period cannot be closed meanwhile. */
945	    private void refuseIfClosed(String sheetId, LocalDate date) {
946	        sheets.lock(sheetId);
947	        periods.refuseIfClosed(sheetId, date);
948	    }
949	
950	    /** Refuse (409) a change to a claim whose editor another user holds open. */
951	    private static void refuseIfLocked(Claim claim, String user) {
952	        if (claim.isLockedFor(user)) {
953	            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT,
954	                    "The claim is being edited by " + claim.getLockedBy());
955	        }
956	    }
957	
958	    /** The number a claim of the amount corrects: none unless the amount is negative, when it must
959	     *  be the number of a SETTLED claim of the same person, or the claim is refused (422). */
960	    private String correctedBy(String sheetId, long personId, BigDecimal amount, String corrects) {
961	        if (amount.signum() >= 0) {
962	            return null;
963	        }
964	        if (corrects == null
965	                || !claims.existsBySheetIdAndPersonIdAndNumberAndStatus(sheetId, personId, corrects, ClaimStatus.SETTLED)) {
966	            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.UNPROCESSABLE_CONTENT,
967	                    "A negative amount must correct a settled claim of the same person");
968	        }
969	        return corrects;
970	    }
971	
972	    /** A claim's reference with surrounding spaces removed: none when blank; refused (409) when
973	     *  another claim on the sheet than the one of the id (null: a new claim) already carries it,
974	     *  comparing without regard to case. */
975	    private String refOf(String sheetId, Long id, String ref) {
976	        if (ref == null || ref.isBlank()) {
977	            return null;
978	        }
979	        String trimmed = ref.trim();
980	        if (claims.existsRef(sheetId, trimmed, id)) {
981	            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT, "The reference " + trimmed + " is already used on the sheet");
982	        }
983	        return trimmed;
984	    }
985	
986	    /** A claim's tags as the form gives them, comma separated: each trimmed and lower-cased, blank
987	     *  ones and repeats dropped, sorted and joined by commas; none when no tag is left. */
988	    static String tagsOf(String tags) {
989	        if (tags == null) {
990	            return null;
991	        }
992	        Set<String> each = new TreeSet<>();
993	        for (String tag : tags.split(",")) {
994	            String t = tag.trim().toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
995	            if (!t.isEmpty()) {
996	                each.add(t);
997	            }
998	        }
999	        return each.isEmpty() ? null : String.join(",", each);
1000	    }
1001	
1002	    /** Keep each of the claim's tags among those ever used on its sheet. */
1003	    public void keepTags(Claim claim) {
1004	        if (claim.getTags() == null) {
1005	            return;
1006	        }
1007	        for (String tag : claim.getTags().split(",")) {
1008	            if (!tagsUsed.existsBySheetIdAndTag(claim.getSheetId(), tag)) {
1009	                tagsUsed.save(new SheetTag(claim.getSheetId(), tag));
1010	            }
1011	        }
1012	    }
1013	
1014	    /** Refuse (422) a claim dated after its person's retirement date. */
1015	    private static void refuseIfRetired(Person person, LocalDate date) {
1016	        if (person.retiredBefore(date)) {
1017	            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.UNPROCESSABLE_CONTENT,
1018	                    "The date is after the person's retirement date");
1019	        }
1020	    }
1021	
1022	    /** Whether a claim counts toward claimed and due totals: only OPEN (or PENDING) and SETTLED ones
1023	     *  do, but not an open one dated within a hold of its person, nor one of a person whose
1024	     *  retirement date the sheet's today has reached, unless bound by a statement, nor one deferred
1025	     *  on the sheet's today. */
1026	    private static boolean counts(Claim c, Person person, LocalDate today) {
1027	        return c.getStatus() == ClaimStatus.SETTLED
1028	                || (c.getStatus().isOpen() && !c.isDeferredOn(today)
1029	                        && (c.isBound() || !(person.heldOn(c.getDate()) || person.retiredOn(today))));
1030	    }
1031	
1032	    /** The due a claim shows: the due fixed when it was settled, else its figure with its late
1033	     *  charge on top, raised to the floor in force on its date. */
1034	    private BigDecimal shownDueOf(Claim claim, Person person) {
1035	        if (claim.getSettledDue() != null) {
1036	            return claim.getSettledDue();
1037	        }
1038	        return flooredOf(claim,
1039	                LateCharge.of(sheets.find(claim.getSheetId())).addTo(claim, person, figureOf(claim, person), roundingOf(claim)));
1040	    }
1041	
1042	    /** A due (null: n/a, which stays n/a) raised to the sheet's floor in force on the claim's date; a
1043	     *  correction's never is. */
1044	    private BigDecimal flooredOf(Claim claim, BigDecimal due) {
1045	        if (due == null || claim.isCorrection()) {
1046	            return due;
1047	        }
1048	        return due.max(sheets.floorOn(claim.getSheetId(), claim.getDate()));
1049	    }
1050	
1051	    /** A claim's figure before any late charge or floor: the one a statement bound it to (null: n/a),
1052	     *  else (unbound, or PENDING) its rate figure. */
1053	    private BigDecimal figureOf(Claim claim, Person person) {
1054	        return claim.isBound() ? claim.getStatedDue() : rateFigureOf(claim, person);
1055	    }
1056	
1057	    /** A person's due-total: the sum of the dues their counting claims show (n/a ones skipped);
1058	     *  null (n/a) when their grade in force on the sheet's today has no rate then, unless a claim
1059	     *  shows a due (a fixed or bound one, or one at the rate of the grade they had on its date). */
1060	    private BigDecimal dueTotalOf(List<Claim> counted, Person person, LocalDate today) {
1061	        List<BigDecimal> dues = counted.stream().map(c -> shownDueOf(c, person)).filter(d -> d != null).toList();
1062	        if (rateChain.findInForce(person.getSheetId(), person.gradeOn(today), today).isEmpty() && dues.isEmpty()) {
1063	            return null;
1064	        }
1065	        return dues.stream().reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO.setScale(2), BigDecimal::add);
1066	    }
1067	
1068	    /** The claim's amount times the rate, in force on the claim's date, of its person's grade then, divided by
1069	     *  100, rounded as its rounding policy has it; null with no rate in force then. */
1070	    private BigDecimal rateFigureOf(Claim claim, Person person) {
1071	        return rateChain.findInForce(claim.getSheetId(), person.gradeOn(claim.getDate()), claim.getDate())
1072	                .map(Rate::getPct)
1073	                .map(pct -> claim.getAmount().multiply(pct).divide(BigDecimal.valueOf(100), 2, roundingOf(claim)))
1074	                .orElse(null);
1075	    }
1076	
1077	    /** How the claim's live figures round: by the sheet's policy date against its date, or for a
1078	     *  correction the date of the claim it corrects. */
1079	    private RoundingMode roundingOf(Claim claim) {
1080	        LocalDate on = claim.getCorrects() == null ? claim.getDate()
1081	                : claims.findFirstBySheetIdAndPersonIdAndNumber(claim.getSheetId(), claim.getPersonId(), claim.getCorrects())
1082	                        .map(Claim::getDate).orElse(claim.getDate());
1083	        return Rounding.of(sheets.find(claim.getSheetId())).on(on);
1084	    }
1085	
1086	    private void record(String event, String user, Person person, Claim claim) {
1087	        record(event, user, person, claim, claim.getNumber());
1088	    }
1089	
1090	    /** Amounts are written as the screen shows them (two decimals), dates as yyyy-mm-dd. */
1091	    private void record(String event, String user, Person person, Claim claim, String number) {
1092	        record(event, user, person, claim, number, "");
1093	    }
1094	
1095	    private void record(String event, String user, Person person, Claim claim, String number, String extra) {
1096	        audit.recordOnCommit(event + " sheet=" + claim.getSheetId() + " by=" + user
1097	                + " person=" + person.getName() + " amount=" + claim.getAmount().setScale(2).toPlainString()
1098	                + " date=" + claim.getDate() + (number != null ? " number=" + number : "") + extra);
1099	    }
1100	
1101	    /** Notify each user watching the person that one of their claims was settled, in the order
1102	     *  they started watching. */
1103	    private void notifyWatchers(String user, Person person, String number) {
1104	        for (PersonWatch w : watches.findByPersonIdOrderByIdAsc(person.getId())) {
1105	            audit.recordOnCommit("NOTIFY sheet=" + person.getSheetId() + " by=" + user + " user=" + w.getUserName()
1106	                    + " person=" + person.getName() + " number=" + number);
1107	        }
1108	    }
1109	
1110	    private static String noteOf(String note) {
1111	        return note == null ? "" : note.trim();
1112	    }
1113	}
